WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.640
- Now, Thanksgiving is
right around the corner,

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:04.740
it's almost here, and it's such
a great time of year, right?

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:07.260
A time to hang out with people you love,

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:09.720
you dig way into too much food.

00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:10.860
You really just kick back.

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:13.170
No pressure, you don't have
to give gifts or anything.

00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:15.480
I'm very excited about
this holiday season.

00:00:15.480 --> 00:00:18.180
My whole family is gonna
be on the Turkey float,

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:20.777
the first float, for the
Macy's Thanksgiving Day parade.

00:00:20.777 --> 00:00:22.020
(audience applauding)

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:23.280
The whole Lopez fam bam.

00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:24.660
We're gonna be bundled up like that,

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:27.900
and I'm also gonna be hosting
part of NBC's live coverage

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:31.830
of Christmas in Rockefeller
Center on the 30th.

00:00:31.830 --> 00:00:34.380
And to really go next level,

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:37.515
I have a brand new movie coming
out on Lifetime this Friday.

00:00:37.515 --> 00:00:38.580
(audience cheers)

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:40.170
Which I'm really excited about.

00:00:40.170 --> 00:00:41.400
I think you all are gonna really like it.

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:43.530
I get to combine so
many things that I love.

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:45.420
I'm dancing and acting,

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:48.180
there's a little romance,
and of course Christmas time.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:50.017
So here's a little sneak peek at

00:00:50.017 --> 00:00:51.930
"Steppin' Into the Holiday."

00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:54.780
- [Billy] You know, maybe this
all happened for a reason.

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:56.640
- When my mom retired,
I took over the studio.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:57.870
Best decision of my life,

00:00:57.870 --> 00:00:59.820
and now we're creating
our own Christmas show.

00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:01.500
Should I add you to the lineup?

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:03.099
- That's not me anymore.

00:01:03.099 --> 00:01:04.587
♪ Chestnuts roastin' ♪

00:01:04.587 --> 00:01:05.790
♪ Champagne toastin' ♪

00:01:05.790 --> 00:01:09.073
- At your core, you're
this guy, not that guy.

00:01:09.073 --> 00:01:10.235
♪ Children wishin' ♪

00:01:10.235 --> 00:01:12.780
♪ Lovers kissin' under mistletoe ♪

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:14.610
- And if that means you are falling

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:17.103
for a woman who doesn't have a publicist,

00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:19.703
then fall.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:21.533
- Oh!

00:01:23.430 --> 00:01:25.143
- Little tease right there.

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:27.720
I get fired from my job,

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:30.960
I go back home cause my
mom's been asking me,

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:32.880
and I reconnect with the family,

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:36.300
and through my nephew and
this young lady named Rae,

00:01:36.300 --> 00:01:37.980
played by Jana Kramer,

00:01:37.980 --> 00:01:39.990
I sort of end up kind of findin' love

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:41.070
and the Christmas spirit again.

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:42.660
You know how those movies goes.

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:44.760
With a little dance
and romance in between,

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:46.410
so hope y'all check it out.

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:48.990
So Kelly always likes to
wrap things up with something

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:50.400
people might be buzzing about,

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:52.650
so thought I'd do the same.

00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:54.162
This is what I'm likin'.

00:01:54.162 --> 00:01:57.390
(electric guitar riff)

00:01:57.390 --> 00:01:58.500
At the beginning of the show,

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:01.687
I told you about my new lifetime
movie, debuting on Friday,

00:02:01.687 --> 00:02:03.540
"Steppin' Into the
Holiday," it's very cool.

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:07.620
I play a character named Billy
Hernandez, aka Billy Holiday.

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:10.170
He stars as a host for a show,

00:02:10.170 --> 00:02:12.990
kinda like "Dancing with the
Stars", but in the movie,

00:02:12.990 --> 00:02:15.180
he gets fired, replaced by his ex,

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:16.980
and things take many turns from there.

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:19.200
It's got romance, it's got comedy,

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:23.914
and I love working and dancing
with my co-star, Jana Kramer.

00:02:23.914 --> 00:02:26.581
(festive music)

00:02:47.474 --> 00:02:50.220
(audience applauding)

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:53.163
We have Jana dialed in now.

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:57.300
Thank you so much for
taking the time to call in.

00:02:57.300 --> 00:03:00.210
I know this, but would you
mind telling everyone else

00:03:00.210 --> 00:03:02.400
about your character in the movie?

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:07.400
- Yeah, so Rae is a dance instructor.

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:11.460
She used to tour for Katy Perry,

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:13.710
and livin' out of a
suitcase wasn't her thing.

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:16.680
So she went home and that's
where she found her maximum joy,

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:21.120
by teaching kids and
being in her hometown.

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:22.170
- Nice, maximum joy,

00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:24.030
one of my favorite expressions from there.

00:03:24.030 --> 00:03:25.410
What about personally,
what plans do you have

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:27.785
for the holidays, other
than watching the movie?

00:03:27.785 --> 00:03:30.570
- (laughs) I'm definitely
gonna watch the movie,

00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:32.460
and then, you know I'm
gonna be honest with you,

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:36.600
this year I was, I have dreaded
this year more than anything

00:03:36.600 --> 00:03:38.700
since my divorce, because
this was gonna be the year

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:42.210
that I didn't have my
kids Christmas morning.

00:03:42.210 --> 00:03:47.210
But I've never looked forward
to a day more now than ever.

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:51.240
I now am gonna get my kids
on Christmas day at noon,

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:53.790
and Santa is actually come the next day,

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:55.530
so we're gonna celebrate
Christmas the next day

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:57.570
so I don't miss out on, you know,

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:58.920
their little feet pitter-pattering

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:01.410
coming down and seeing
the presents from Santa.

00:04:01.410 --> 00:04:04.440
So I'm excited to create
our own memory this year,

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:06.240
and I'm really lookin' forward to that.

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:08.190
- Oh, that's awesome.

00:04:08.190 --> 00:04:10.230
I'm so glad that worked out right there.

00:04:10.230 --> 00:04:11.790
Thank you so much, Jana.

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:14.430
I'm liking your post
right now. (kiss sound)

00:04:14.430 --> 00:04:15.263
That's awesome.

00:04:16.237 --> 00:04:18.660
"Steppin' Into the Holiday"
premieres this Friday night

00:04:18.660 --> 00:04:21.420
on Lifetime, hope you
check it out and enjoy.

00:04:21.420 --> 00:04:22.710
Alright, now.

00:04:22.710 --> 00:04:25.380
We've hit the point where
Kelly usually gives the guest

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:26.370
a thousand dollars,

00:04:26.370 --> 00:04:29.400
courtesy of the shows
season-long partner, Pilot Pen,

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:32.310
makers of G2, the go-to pen
of the Kelly Clarkson Show,

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:35.940
but I think it'd be, it'd
show way too much favoritism

00:04:35.940 --> 00:04:37.080
if I give it to Jana, right?

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:40.785
So today, the money's going
to someone in the audience.

00:04:40.785 --> 00:04:42.720
(audience cheers)

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:45.870
So if everyone can
please get up real quick,

00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:47.400
and look under their chairs,

00:04:47.400 --> 00:04:51.060
because someone has a check
taped under their chair,

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:55.207
and is gonna come up
with a thousand bucks.

00:04:55.207 --> 00:05:00.207
(Mario cheers)
(audience cheers)

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:03.450
Congratulations, what's your name?

00:05:03.450 --> 00:05:04.500
- Kaylee.

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:06.757
Hi Kaylee. Congrats!

00:05:06.757 --> 00:05:10.002
- Thank you! Thank you so much!

00:05:10.002 --> 00:05:10.890
- What do you,

00:05:10.890 --> 00:05:12.450
what do you plan to do with the money?

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:14.100
- I'm going to Bahrain next year,

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:16.470
gonna travel with my husband.

00:05:16.470 --> 00:05:17.669
- There you go.

00:05:17.669 --> 00:05:18.743
- [Kaylee] Yeah!

00:05:18.743 --> 00:05:21.090
- Spend it on the vacation, good for you.

00:05:21.090 --> 00:05:22.570
Congrats and happy holidays to you.

00:05:22.570 --> 00:05:24.135
Nice!
- Thank you!

00:05:24.135 --> 00:05:27.330
And a big thanks to all
our guests this hour,

00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:30.360
Jonathan Majors, Christina
Jackson, who were in a lasso,

00:05:30.360 --> 00:05:33.720
Angelica Ortega, the P.S. 14
choir, Natalie Pascarella,

00:05:33.720 --> 00:05:36.960
and all our friends over at NBC4 New York,

00:05:36.960 --> 00:05:39.450
Alex Aster, and Lawrence Zarian.

00:05:39.450 --> 00:05:42.993
As Kelly says, have a great
day and if it's not, change it.

